<title>GERMANY: Reuters 2nd ex-Frankfurt Americas/Africa cargo report.</title>
<headline>Reuters 2nd ex-Frankfurt Americas/Africa cargo report.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the current average ex-Frankfurt (FRA) German mark air cargo rates per kg for a 100kg shipment, with a volume to weight ratio of six-to-one.</p>
<p>		  June 20	  Mar 27</p>
<p>			 NORTH AMERICA</p>
<p>    FRA-NYC   1.75	     1.80</p>
<p>    FRA-CHI   1.75	     1.80</p>
<p>    FRA-LAX   2.10	     2.10</p>
<p>    FRA-MIA   2.00	     2.05</p>
<p>    FRA-ATL   1.95	     1.95</p>
<p>    FRA-TOR   1.95	     1.95</p>
<p>			 LATIN AMERICA</p>
<p>    FRA-SAO   5.15	     5.20</p>
<p>    FRA-BUE   5.25	     5.30</p>
<p>    FRA-SCL   5.25	     5.30</p>
<p>    FRA-BOG   3.75	     3.75</p>
<p>    FRA-MEX   3.30	     3.30</p>
<p>			 AFRICA</p>
<p>    FRA-JNB   3.95	     4.00</p>
<p>    FRA-HRE   3.80	     3.80</p>
<p>* The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuter journalists on a confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents based at or near Frankfurt Airport.</p>
<p>* All prices are quoted in German marks.</p>
<p>* The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices, including standard, discount and spot rates, and are indicative of current market activity. - Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
</text>
